│ patch_name               │ grouped_symmetric_ansatz                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The structural redesign moves from a global collective parameter sharing scheme to a      │
│                          │ grouped-symmetric architecture. By splitting the 8-qubit register into two groups (even   │
│                          │ and odd wires) and assigning shared parameters within these groups, the model increases   │
│                          │ its expressivity while maintaining high parameter efficiency. The entanglement strategy   │
│                          │ is also updated: it combines a fixed circular CZ-chain for global connectivity with       │
│                          │ trainable long-range CRY gates that allow the network to learn the strength of            │
│                          │ correlations between non-adjacent qubits. This approach maintains a low parameter count   │
│                          │ (38 total) to prevent overfitting, which was the key to the success of the previous       │
│                          │ iteration, while providing enough flexibility to capture more complex feature             │
│                          │ dependencies.                                                                             │
