│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parity_mix_entangler                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This edit keeps the ansatz at the same parameter budget as the current winner, but makes  │
│                          │ it more expressive by breaking the global qubit symmetry into even/odd sublattices and by │
│                          │ replacing the purely diagonal entangling scaffold with a mixed CZ/CNOT pattern.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - The current block uses the same angle on all 8 qubits, which is very                    │
│                          │ parameter-efficient but can underfit subtle class structure.                              │
│                          │ - Even/odd parameter sharing adds just enough asymmetry to capture localized correlations │
│                          │ without inflating the model.                                                              │
│                          │ - Interleaving CNOT with CZ gives both phase entanglement and amplitude mixing, which is  │
│                          │ often beneficial when the data map is phase-based and the readout is in the Z basis.      │
│                          │ - The gate count stays compact and the number of trainable parameters per block remains   │
│                          │ 4, so the model should preserve the strong generalization and optimization behavior while │
│                          │ improving fit.                                                                            │
