╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhance_expressiveness_with_individual_tuning                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves excellent performance (score 0.45) with a highly             │
│                          │ parameter-efficient collective parameter sharing strategy. However, there is room to      │
│                          │ improve test accuracy and expressiveness while maintaining efficiency.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key observation from metrics:**                                                         │
│                          │ - Current: 26 params, test_acc=0.90, generalization_gap=0.01                              │
│                          │ - The parameter sharing yields excellent generalization, but may limit expressiveness     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed enhancement:**                                                                 │
│                          │ Add individual RX rotations after the collective RY input mixer and before the collective │
│                          │ RZ phase. This allows per-qubit fine-tuning early in the circuit without sacrificing the  │
│                          │ parameter-sharing benefits of the later stages.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Rationale:**                                                                            │
│                          │ 1. Adds only 8 new parameters per block (individually tuned RX on each qubit), bringing   │
│                          │ total to ~74 params                                                                       │
│                          │ 2. Provides expressiveness boost by allowing asymmetric contributions early in the ansatz │
│                          │ 3. Maintains collective phases and output stages which were working well                  │
│                          │ 4. Early individual tuning can help the circuit adapt to dataset asymmetries while        │
│                          │ collective later stages preserve good generalization                                      │
│                          │ 5. Expected to improve test accuracy from 0.90 toward 0.92-0.94 range while keeping       │
│                          │ generalization gap low                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This follows the pattern seen in prior program 2 which achieved test_acc=0.87 with 146    │
│                          │ params; we're finding a better middle ground.                                             │
